<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40452" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rătĭōcĭnātīvus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In rhet., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			reasoning</i>, <i>syllogistic</i>, <i>ratiocinative</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Inv. 1, 13, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 1, 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">status,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7,
					8, 3</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 3, 6, 46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">61</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 10,
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In gram.: ratiocinativa conjunctio, <i>serving for
				inference</i>, <i>illative</i>, as ergo, igitur,
					<i><span class="en">Diom. p. 410</span></i> P.</div>
